use std
into view.amni

Imports: os, web, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d.

Globals: `P f32[10240]` (pose: ten floats per driven node), `C f32[16]` (camera), `N byte[16384]` (node names), `Q i32[1024]` (glTF node indices from the page), `M f32[16]` (placement matrix, column-major, starts as identity), `B int[1024]` (global node per driven node, starts all -1), `var nb = 0`, `var asset = -1`, `var item = -1`, `var sw = 0`, `var sh = 0`.

Declare `extern fn hv_f32(id i32, xs f32[:]);`, `extern fn hv_i32(id i32, xs i32[:]);` and `extern fn hv_bytes(id i32, xs byte[:]);`.

`main()` shares the buffers with the page: `hv_f32(0, P[..])`, `hv_f32(1, C[..])`, `hv_bytes(2, N[..])`, `hv_i32(3, Q[..])`, `hv_f32(4, M[..])`. Set `gltf::lazy_pixels = true`. With `a = args()`, load `a[1]` with `gltf::load` into `asset` (negative: print "view: " plus `gltf::error()` and return). Open the canvas with `gfx::open("amni companion", 640, 800)` (false: print "view: " plus `gfx::error()` and return). `item = s3d::add(asset)`; `s3d::place(item, gfx::mat4_identity)`. Set `s3d::view` to an `s3d::Camera` with eye (0, 1.2, 3.5), target (0, 0.9, 0), up (0, 1, 0), fov_y 0.5236, near 0.05, far 100. Set `s3d::sun.shadows = true`. Fill `C` with eye, target and fov as C[0..7] = 0, 1.2, 3.5, 0, 0.9, 0, 0.5236. Let `z = gfx::screen_size()`; set `sw = z.x as int`, `sh = z.y as int`; `s3d::init(sw, sh)`; then `web::frames(true)`.

`export fn hv_bones(len i32) i32` splits `N[0..len]` on newline bytes (10); for each non-empty name in order, at index k below 1024, set `B[k] = gltf::find_node(asset, name)`; set `nb` to the number of names; return how many had `B[k] >= 0` as i32.

`export fn hv_nodes(n i32) i32` drives the asset's own nodes by glTF index: for each k below n and below 1024, with `q = Q[k] as int`, set `B[k] = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first + q` when `q >= 0` and `q < gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count`, else -1; set `nb` to n clamped to 1024; return how many were set as i32.

`export fn hv_stop()` calls `web::frames(false)` and `gfx::close()`.

`export fn he_frame(t real)`: return if `gfx::frame()` is false. For each k below nb with `B[k] >= 0`, with `o = k * 10`, call `s3d::set_node(item, B[k], float3 { P[o], P[o + 1], P[o + 2] }, linalg::Quat { P[o + 3], P[o + 4], P[o + 5], P[o + 6] }, float3 { P[o + 7], P[o + 8], P[o + 9] })`. Place the avatar with `s3d::place(item, gfx::mat4 { float4 { M[0], M[1], M[2], M[3] }, float4 { M[4], M[5], M[6], M[7] }, float4 { M[8], M[9], M[10], M[11] }, float4 { M[12], M[13], M[14], M[15] } })`. Set `s3d::view` to an `s3d::Camera` with eye (C[0], C[1], C[2]), target (C[3], C[4], C[5]), up (0, 1, 0), fov_y C[6], near 0.05, far 100. Let `z = gfx::screen_size()`; when `z.x as int != sw` or `z.y as int != sh`, update sw and sh and call `s3d::init(sw, sh)`. Finally `s3d::render(gfx::screen())`.
